\import{fcap-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\tag{fcap}
\tag{spin}
\tag{representation-theory}

\taxon{Proposition}
\title{Clifford multiplication gives the triality trilinear}

\p{Complexify the compact model and use the split rank-four exterior
carrier #{S=\bigwedge W} with a chosen top form
#{\operatorname{vol}=e_1\wedge e_2\wedge e_3\wedge e_4}. Define

##{B(s,t)=[\operatorname{rev}_{\wedge}(s)\wedge t]_{\operatorname{vol}}.}

In degree four this form is symmetric; its restrictions #{B_+} and
#{B_-} to #{S^+} and #{S^-} are nondegenerate. Each creation operator and
each polar-dual contraction operator is individually self-adjoint for
#{B}. Thus the adjoint of Clifford multiplication by #{x} is
multiplication by #{\operatorname{rev}(x)}, and actual Spin elements
preserve #{B}.}

\p{For #{v\in V}, #{s_+\in S^+}, and #{s_-\in S^-}, put

##{F(v,s_+,s_-)=B_-(\rho(v)s_+,s_-).}

Clifford covariance of #{\rho(v)} and invariance of #{B} give

##{F(\pi(g)v,\rho_+(g)s_+,\rho_-(g)s_-)=F(v,s_+,s_-)
\qquad(g\in\Spin_8).}

The form is nonzero: with the displayed orientation,

##{F(e_1,1,e_2\wedge e_3\wedge e_4)=1.}

This is an explicit invariant tensor
#{V\otimes S^+\otimes S^-\to\mathbb C}; changing the chosen top form
rescales it.}

\p{It is unique up to scalar. The full odd Clifford range is

##{\operatorname{Hom}(S^+,S^-)\oplus
\operatorname{Hom}(S^-,S^+).}

Under equivariant antisymmetrization its degrees are #{1,3,5,7}.
Multiplication by the normalized Clifford volume element of the
eight-dimensional space #{V} exchanges degrees #{k} and #{8-k};
projecting to either chirality block therefore gives

##{\operatorname{Hom}(S^+,S^-)\simeq V\oplus\bigwedge^3V.}

The two summands are nonisomorphic irreducible #{\Spin_8}-modules, so
#{V} occurs exactly once. The nondegenerate forms identify invariant
trilinears with
#{\operatorname{Hom}_{\Spin_8}(V,S^+\otimes S^-)}, which is therefore
one-dimensional.}

\p{\citet{Chapter 5, Proposition 5.7, pp. 35--36}{adams1996exceptional}
states the invariant trilinear and proves the required multiplicity-one
decomposition.}

\p{\citet{Section 20.3, pp. 313--314}{fulton2004representation}
independently construct the Clifford-multiplication trilinear in the
complex modules. The displayed top-form formula fixes its normalization
in the FCAP creation--contraction convention. It does not assert a normed
composition algebra or an order-three isometry of the tensor.}
